  "id": "corpus-08-assembly-verification",
  "title": "Assembly verification \u2014 junctions, not interiors",
  "updatedAt": "2026-07-14T12:00:00.000Z",
  "storage": {
    "type": "database",
    "table": "pages",
    "id": "corpus-08-assembly-verification"
  },
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly verification \u2014 junctions, not interiors"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Directive \u2014 Verify the fusion sites specifically, because that is where Golden Gate fails and where colony PCR is blind."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What colony PCR cannot see"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A flanking-primer PCR gives a correctly sized band whenever the parts are present in the right order. It says nothing about whether each 4-base fusion scar is correct, and a single-base scar error shifts the downstream reading frame."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sanger across all four junctions of the entry-07 product, using primers that sit in the parts and read INTO the scars. Junction-spanning reads only; interior reads are not evidence."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "mention",
            "attrs": {
              "id": "sample-161979b5",
              "label": "ODC_0001 (run control)",
              "entityType": "sequence",
              "entityId": "sample-161979b5",
              "path": "sequences/kits/open-plasmids/ODC_0001",
              "contentHash": null,
              "objectUuid": null
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is included as a sequencing-run control to separate a bad read from a bad construct."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Result"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "All four junctions exact. One clone carried a silent interior single-nucleotide difference in "
          },
          {
            "type": "mention",
            "attrs": {
              "id": "sample-694681f1",
              "label": "E1010m (mRFP)",
              "entityType": "sequence",
              "entityId": "sample-694681f1",
              "path": "sequences/kits/moclo-cidar/E1010m_CD",
              "contentHash": null,
              "objectUuid": null
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " relative to the reference, attributable to the part stock rather than to assembly, and it was retained as the working clone with the difference recorded."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
